      "canonicalConceptId": "concept:162b2fdb2b2733b5f3e691ba2cc5ae401c3ce430e1fd22b5c4343b2870b78290",
      "text": "ManagedSubscribe moves the replay checkpoint to Salesforce, while the client remains responsible for explicitly committing its processed position. Resumption follows a successful checkpoint. Administrative stopping resets that position, which differs from an ordinary client disconnect. Commit acknowledgements may combine requests, and empty event batches can supply positions to commit. Current Salesforce references still label this capability Beta. For case alerting, the lifecycle therefore requires deliberate commit handling and a tested stop/restart procedure. An independent implementation reports a prolonged slot hold after network failures; its timing is an observation rather than a service guarantee.",
